WEBVTT

00:01.200 --> 00:05.660
We’ve returned from our trip,
and life is back to normal.

00:05.660 --> 00:08.990
Normal... That’s kind of nice.

00:09.970 --> 00:14.000
A normal where Ayako-san’s by my side...

00:14.000 --> 00:18.940
That almost sounds like too much to ask.

00:36.140 --> 00:41.260
Today I shout out another good morning courageously

00:41.260 --> 00:46.560
The sparkling chime of hope is resounding

00:47.050 --> 00:52.140
The gentle sun is always

00:52.140 --> 00:57.660
Blessing the late coming sensation of the two of them

00:57.950 --> 01:02.880
To fall in love with a goddess is the best!

01:03.090 --> 01:12.950
Even if she is a beatrice I can't control this throbbing feeling

01:12.950 --> 01:13.800
L·O·V·E

01:13.800 --> 01:15.550
I love you MA·MO·RU!

01:15.550 --> 01:17.090
These overflowing feelings

01:17.090 --> 01:19.790
Take them high into the sky

01:19.790 --> 01:24.680
Please grant me my dazzling and sparkling dream

01:24.680 --> 01:26.480
That's right MA·MO·RU!

01:26.480 --> 01:28.010
Only for you

01:28.010 --> 01:30.680
I will show you my power of miracles

01:30.680 --> 01:32.950
I will surely, surely swear

01:32.950 --> 01:38.900
I will not end my Shining Love

01:57.030 --> 02:00.740
Curry pilaf, fried chicken, and potato salad.

02:01.570 --> 02:04.110
All my favorites!

02:04.110 --> 02:07.710
Ayako-san, I’m always so happy
when you make me lunch.

02:07.710 --> 02:09.150
It’s great!

02:09.150 --> 02:11.350
What do you mean?

02:11.350 --> 02:14.490
I make it because I want to.

02:14.490 --> 02:18.160
Just thinking that you’ll eat it makes me happy...

02:18.160 --> 02:20.170
I-I mean...

02:20.170 --> 02:24.800
<i>But I don’t know if I can always let her cook, without doing something in return.</i>

02:24.800 --> 02:26.470
I know! Ayako-san...

02:26.470 --> 02:28.770
Are you free tomorrow? It’s Saturday.

02:28.770 --> 02:29.830
Tomorrow?

02:29.830 --> 02:31.440
Yeah, sure.

02:31.440 --> 02:34.260
Then come eat at my place!

02:36.210 --> 02:37.480
Ayako-san?

02:37.480 --> 02:39.940
A-At your house?

02:40.830 --> 02:42.180
Eat lunch?!

02:43.350 --> 02:48.350
Together with Brother

02:49.490 --> 02:52.790
I refuse to believe it!

02:52.790 --> 02:54.730
I will not believe it!

02:54.730 --> 02:57.150
I refuse to believe it!

03:00.320 --> 03:09.610
Happy /
Embarrassed
Home
Visit

03:01.630 --> 03:05.400
“Special Edition: Witch Beatrice Visits Yoshimura Household.”

03:05.400 --> 03:08.170
“At last, the two are introduced to each other’s families.”

03:08.170 --> 03:10.340
Looks pretty good.

03:10.340 --> 03:12.310
Nice work, Mitsuki.

03:12.310 --> 03:16.000
Yagi-sempai helped out a lot.

03:17.210 --> 03:19.630
But it’s pretty nice, isn’t it?

03:19.630 --> 03:21.870
She’s meeting his family...

03:21.870 --> 03:25.410
But she’s met his little sister, Itsumi, many times.

03:25.410 --> 03:27.640
And she’s met his mom, too.

03:27.640 --> 03:30.300
But this is different!

03:30.300 --> 03:32.440
She’s being introduced to his family.

03:32.440 --> 03:35.240
They’re like an official couple!

03:36.530 --> 03:39.600
Um, Um... What is this?

03:42.490 --> 03:43.570
Coming.

03:48.080 --> 03:51.050
Where will she enter from today?

03:51.050 --> 03:53.050
I’m all set.

03:58.560 --> 04:01.530
Sorry to keep repeating the same scene,

04:01.530 --> 04:04.840
but the third student council room boasts
five times the armor of the last!

04:04.840 --> 04:07.170
She won’t get in today!

04:07.170 --> 04:08.500
She isn’t there?

04:11.900 --> 04:14.640
Yoshimura, behind you!

04:19.530 --> 04:20.960
Yoshimura!

04:25.280 --> 04:26.220
Hi!

04:27.050 --> 04:28.080
Ayako!

04:28.080 --> 04:33.080
You should probably conceal your
violent side in front of Mamoru’s mother.

04:33.080 --> 04:34.890
It might affect your future!

04:34.890 --> 04:37.880
I was going to interview them tomorrow,

04:37.880 --> 04:41.920
but since that would be rude to his family,
I guess I’ll pass this time.

04:41.920 --> 04:43.040
Of course you will!

04:46.240 --> 04:48.050
This is no good.

04:48.050 --> 04:49.590
Let’s move on!

04:49.590 --> 04:50.580
Next!

04:56.480 --> 04:59.730
Ayako-san, I’m not giving up!

04:59.730 --> 05:03.590
Someday, your smile will be mine...

05:06.200 --> 05:08.340
Ayako-san!

05:08.340 --> 05:09.620
Snap

05:09.620 --> 05:11.900
Ow!

05:12.650 --> 05:18.050
Miss, what are you wearing tomorrow?

05:18.050 --> 05:20.460
If it’s your first visit to his home,

05:20.460 --> 05:21.970
you should wear something formal and nice...

05:21.970 --> 05:25.380
Ah, Kikukawa-san, how did you know about it?

05:25.380 --> 05:26.710
Well, you see...

05:26.710 --> 05:29.410
Kikukawa, don’t say any more than necessary.

05:29.410 --> 05:32.150
Um, Ayako-san?

05:32.150 --> 05:33.690
I’m sorry.

05:33.690 --> 05:36.260
This has become a big thing.

05:36.260 --> 05:39.540
It isn’t anything you should apologize for.

05:39.540 --> 05:43.470
And I... Um... I’m really looking forward to it.

05:43.470 --> 05:44.650
Really?

05:44.650 --> 05:45.700
That’s great!

05:45.700 --> 05:48.960
Itsumi’s cooking isn’t anything special,

05:48.960 --> 05:50.470
but it tastes good.

05:50.470 --> 05:54.620
She’s been working on it since elementary school.

05:54.620 --> 05:56.530
It’s really nice of her.

05:56.530 --> 05:58.170
I dunno.

05:58.170 --> 06:01.220
Our mom isn’t very good at cooking.

06:01.220 --> 06:04.320
Itsumi got sick of eating Mom’s food,
saying she’d prepare it herself.

06:04.320 --> 06:05.020
I see.

06:05.020 --> 06:08.590
So really, it isn’t a big a deal.

06:08.590 --> 06:13.220
If you came over, Itsumi and my mom
would both really like it.

06:14.150 --> 06:15.860
Then...

06:15.860 --> 06:19.150
I guess I’ll be there.

06:30.160 --> 06:31.210
Mom?

06:31.210 --> 06:32.730
What happened?

06:32.730 --> 06:34.410
Oh, Mamoru!

06:34.410 --> 06:36.080
We’re cleaning!

06:36.080 --> 06:38.500
I’d planned to clean up.

06:38.500 --> 06:41.700
I’ll take care of it. You relax.

06:41.700 --> 06:42.830
Really?

06:42.830 --> 06:45.320
OK. I’ll go do the laundry!

06:45.320 --> 06:46.520
Oh, right!

06:46.520 --> 06:48.930
Don’t put up my underwear and stuff today.

06:48.930 --> 06:50.760
Why not?

06:50.760 --> 06:53.130
It’s a perfect underwear day!

06:53.130 --> 06:55.370
Because it’s embarrassing!

06:55.370 --> 06:56.680
Right, right.

07:02.430 --> 07:03.710
Itsumi!

07:06.410 --> 07:08.100
How’s it going?

07:08.100 --> 07:11.490
Ah... It’s going OK...

07:15.280 --> 07:16.840
Hey, Mom.

07:16.840 --> 07:18.160
What is it, Mamoru?

07:18.160 --> 07:20.070
Is something wrong with Itsumi?

07:20.070 --> 07:22.180
She seemed kinda spacey.

07:22.180 --> 07:23.890
Lately, she’s always like that.

07:25.030 --> 07:26.890
I hadn’t noticed at all.

07:26.890 --> 07:29.980
You’ve been busy recently.

07:29.980 --> 07:31.300
I’m sorry.

07:31.300 --> 07:34.860
It’s fine. It’s fine.
She’s at that age.

07:34.860 --> 07:37.200
Don’t worry about it!

07:37.200 --> 07:39.540
Girls get like that.

07:39.540 --> 07:40.600
Yeah?

07:40.240 --> 07:41.210
Mamoru

07:40.600 --> 07:41.210
Yup.

07:44.820 --> 07:46.960
I need to hurry.

07:47.750 --> 07:49.810
Can I help?

07:49.810 --> 07:53.090
No, it’ll just take longer overall.

07:54.360 --> 07:56.400
What are we having today?

07:56.400 --> 07:58.960
Red rice, okashira-tsuki tai,

07:58.960 --> 08:01.620
chicken with veggies inside,

08:01.620 --> 08:03.100
pumpkin potage,

08:03.100 --> 08:04.030
and dessert.

08:04.030 --> 08:06.070
Wow, that’s a lot.

08:06.070 --> 08:09.480
It’s like Christmas and my birthday put together!

08:09.480 --> 08:13.480
Well, we can’t serve her leftovers.

08:13.480 --> 08:14.930
Oh, right.

08:14.930 --> 08:15.930
Thank you.

08:15.930 --> 08:16.920
It’s nothing.

08:18.700 --> 08:21.180
OK, I’m going to keep cleaning.

08:53.840 --> 08:56.020
The onion’s getting in my eyes today...

08:56.020 --> 08:57.690
Kikukawa!

08:58.940 --> 09:00.220
Excuse me.

09:00.590 --> 09:02.430
Wh-What do you think?

09:02.430 --> 09:06.640
Miss, you aren’t going to a ball or anything.

09:06.640 --> 09:10.030
Jeez, I don’t know what to do...

09:10.030 --> 09:12.730
I remember how my wife looked

09:12.730 --> 09:16.010
when she first visited my house.

09:16.010 --> 09:18.380
That white dress...

09:18.380 --> 09:19.110
White...

09:19.110 --> 09:21.240
So pure and beautiful...

09:21.240 --> 09:26.210
When I close my eyes, I can still see it.

09:26.530 --> 09:31.490
Of course, my wife’s not nearly as beautiful as you.

09:31.490 --> 09:34.530
But maybe she was back then...

09:38.430 --> 09:39.540
Itsumi?

09:39.540 --> 09:40.420
What’s wrong?

09:43.930 --> 09:46.440
We’ll just eat the other stuff.

09:46.440 --> 09:48.340
There was okashira-tsuki tai?

09:52.400 --> 09:55.500
But see, we have the red rice.

09:55.500 --> 09:58.300
Bwan~

09:56.810 --> 09:58.320
Watered rice?

09:58.320 --> 10:00.890
I added too much water.

10:05.200 --> 10:06.290
It’s Ayako-san!

10:06.290 --> 10:07.000
Be right there!

10:11.530 --> 10:12.810
Ayako-san...

10:14.030 --> 10:17.150
Thank you for inviting me, Mamoru.

10:20.790 --> 10:23.520
Then I’ll be back later to pick you up.

10:27.980 --> 10:30.250
Ayako-san, actually...

10:30.250 --> 10:31.350
I’m sorry.

10:31.350 --> 10:33.780
We aren’t ready yet.

10:33.780 --> 10:35.220
Want to get takeout?

10:35.220 --> 10:35.790
Sushi?

10:35.790 --> 10:36.510
Eel?

10:36.510 --> 10:39.080
Why not remake lunch with the ingredients we have?

10:39.080 --> 10:41.480
OK, I’ll help.

10:41.480 --> 10:46.110
No, we can’t feed you leftovers.

10:46.110 --> 10:48.060
And your clothes will get stained!

10:48.060 --> 10:51.900
I brought this, just in case.

10:53.200 --> 10:55.770
You look wonderful, Ayako-san!

10:55.770 --> 10:59.440
Mamoru, you and Mom go buy what we need.

11:00.600 --> 11:02.340
I wanted sushi, too...

11:02.340 --> 11:05.290
Let’s get the shopping done quickly.

11:09.340 --> 11:12.980
All right... First, wash and peel these.

11:12.980 --> 11:14.370
OK.

11:16.790 --> 11:19.360
May I ask what we’re making?

11:19.360 --> 11:21.980
Pickled potatoes, omelet with cheese,

11:21.980 --> 11:23.200
Japanese Salisbury steak,

11:23.200 --> 11:24.190
and curry soup.

11:24.190 --> 11:27.000
All Mamoru’s favorites.

11:28.300 --> 11:31.600
Yeah, she’d know what her boyfriend likes.

11:31.600 --> 11:32.750
B-Boyfriend...

11:35.710 --> 11:38.420
It was in the survey.

11:38.420 --> 11:39.990
Survey?

11:39.990 --> 11:45.310
Yes. After we’d just met,
I had him fill out a survey.

11:45.310 --> 11:48.590
About his favorite foods and colors...

11:50.300 --> 11:51.950
<i>White?</i>

11:51.950 --> 11:53.730
<i>His favorite color...</i>

11:54.950 --> 11:56.400
Can I ask you something?

11:56.400 --> 11:57.640
What is it?

11:57.640 --> 11:59.870
When he answered the question about his family,

11:59.870 --> 12:02.280
he said he had a mom and little sister.

12:02.280 --> 12:03.450
That’s right.

12:03.450 --> 12:07.380
Our family’s Mom, Mamoru, and me.

12:07.380 --> 12:10.400
I know this is rude...

12:10.400 --> 12:13.200
But what happened to your father?

12:13.200 --> 12:15.140
Mamoru didn’t tell you?

12:15.140 --> 12:18.450
No, and somehow I just can’t find
the right time to ask...

12:18.450 --> 12:20.090
He left.

12:21.930 --> 12:24.770
When Mamoru and I were little,

12:24.770 --> 12:26.880
he said something stupid about

12:26.880 --> 12:30.370
how a man couldn’t be tied
down by a family, and he left.

12:30.370 --> 12:32.180
I-I see...

12:32.180 --> 12:35.040
He must live freely.

12:35.040 --> 12:38.070
Ayako-san, you’re good at cooking.

12:38.070 --> 12:39.270
Am I?

12:39.270 --> 12:40.800
You’re a rich girl,

12:40.800 --> 12:43.680
so I thought maybe you hadn’t
touched a knife before.

12:43.680 --> 12:47.080
Since childhood, I’ve studied many things.

12:47.080 --> 12:49.020
Including cooking.

12:49.020 --> 12:51.840
Japanese, Chinese, French, Italian...

12:51.840 --> 12:53.590
I can do most of them.

12:53.590 --> 12:56.180
Wow, I’m jealous.

12:56.180 --> 12:58.380
I’m jealous of you.

12:58.380 --> 13:00.210
Why?

13:00.210 --> 13:05.390
Until I met Mamoru, I’d never cooked for anyone.

13:05.390 --> 13:09.170
Once in a while, my grandfather would come home, and I’d cook for him, but that was it.

13:09.690 --> 13:14.750
So I’m jealous that you get to
cook for your family daily.

13:17.850 --> 13:19.690
Ayako-san...

13:21.300 --> 13:24.860
Why are you dating someone like Mamoru?!

13:24.860 --> 13:28.030
You’ve grown up, Mamoru.

13:28.030 --> 13:29.470
No, I haven’t.

13:29.470 --> 13:31.210
I’m still short.

13:31.210 --> 13:34.950
But you’ve grown up, compared to
how you were at birth.

13:34.950 --> 13:36.430
I suppose so...

13:37.220 --> 13:38.980
You’re so cute, Mamoru!

13:38.980 --> 13:40.260
Stop it, Mom.

13:40.260 --> 13:42.440
Aw, come on...

13:43.070 --> 13:45.740
Ever since we were little, the neighbors always said

13:45.740 --> 13:51.940
that Mamoru was cuter, and I was cooler.

13:52.780 --> 13:54.590
Is that funny?

13:54.590 --> 13:55.650
No...

13:55.650 --> 13:57.960
Mamoru’s unfair.

13:57.960 --> 13:59.390
Unfair?

14:00.720 --> 14:04.630
When we were young, we used to fight a lot.

14:04.630 --> 14:08.140
Actually, we still do sometimes.

14:08.140 --> 14:10.780
But usually...

14:14.970 --> 14:17.170
That smile!

14:17.170 --> 14:20.880
It makes you wonder how he can smile so gently.

14:20.880 --> 14:23.430
That sparkling smile...

14:23.430 --> 14:27.620
Whenever I saw it, I somehow stopped being mad.

14:36.680 --> 14:40.230
Yeah, that smile of his isn’t fair.

14:40.230 --> 14:44.540
Was the smile what got you?

14:44.540 --> 14:45.540
N-No!

14:46.250 --> 14:47.910
Not that it matters.

14:57.820 --> 15:01.950
Mamoru must have been cute when he was little.

15:01.950 --> 15:06.290
Actually, he got bullied a lot.

15:08.330 --> 15:11.330
He isn’t good at dealing with that stuff.

15:11.330 --> 15:14.070
So I was worried about him,

15:14.070 --> 15:16.540
and I tried to help.

15:17.630 --> 15:23.840
But the next thing I knew, he’d usually
have taken care of things himself.

15:23.840 --> 15:27.950
And sometimes, he helped me.

15:28.900 --> 15:30.830
That’s just like him.

15:30.830 --> 15:32.680
He’s just not fair.

15:32.680 --> 15:35.660
That smile makes you forgive everything.

15:35.660 --> 15:39.330
I want to hear more about how he was as a kid.

15:42.290 --> 15:45.660
How long ago was that?

15:55.330 --> 15:59.930
I woke up to a big thunderstorm,
and I was so scared...

16:07.590 --> 16:08.650
<i>Itsumi?</i>

16:11.780 --> 16:13.280
<i>Come here.</i>

16:20.800 --> 16:24.600
<i>This is a magic towel.</i>

16:24.600 --> 16:27.340
<i>A magic towel?</i>

16:27.340 --> 16:31.710
<i>If you hold it, it’ll protect you.</i>

17:00.830 --> 17:04.680
<i>That’s a secret between Mamoru and me.</i>

17:05.840 --> 17:09.160
<i>I won’t tell anyone.</i>

17:16.420 --> 17:17.990
Do you have anything to wipe it up?

17:17.990 --> 17:21.310
U-Um, by the washer...

17:28.590 --> 17:30.200
Are you OK, Itsumi-san?

17:30.200 --> 17:32.110
Did you burn your foot?

17:32.570 --> 17:33.570
It’s fine.

17:33.570 --> 17:34.070
It’s nothing.

17:34.070 --> 17:34.740
It’s not fine!

17:44.990 --> 17:49.430
You really are good at everything.

17:49.430 --> 17:51.250
That’s not true.

17:52.580 --> 17:53.700
Does it hurt?

17:54.520 --> 17:56.260
It’s all right.

18:08.420 --> 18:09.790
Beatrice?

18:17.200 --> 18:19.980
It reminds me of when I was little...

18:19.980 --> 18:21.590
Little?

18:21.590 --> 18:26.930
I don’t know why. But somehow, it does.

18:30.770 --> 18:32.090
It doesn’t hurt?

18:32.090 --> 18:34.060
It’s healed!

18:34.060 --> 18:36.180
I’m so glad.

18:39.040 --> 18:39.900
What?

18:39.900 --> 18:40.740
Does it still hurt?

18:40.740 --> 18:47.450
Th-Th-That’s Mamoru’s favorite towel,
from when he was a kid!

18:47.450 --> 18:51.020
If he doesn’t have it, he can’t sleep!

18:54.280 --> 18:55.560
What should I do?

18:55.560 --> 18:57.090
I... I...

18:57.090 --> 18:59.360
I ruined his favorite towel!

18:59.360 --> 19:00.660
I’m horrible!

19:00.660 --> 19:04.130
Can you do something with beatrice?

19:05.520 --> 19:06.960
Maybe.

19:06.960 --> 19:08.700
I’ll try.

19:08.700 --> 19:11.350
If it goes well, I can make it as clean as new.

19:11.350 --> 19:12.430
Wait!

19:13.070 --> 19:14.560
Wait.

19:14.560 --> 19:15.410
Please...

19:16.710 --> 19:18.610
Don’t clean it.

19:22.280 --> 19:24.190
Please.

19:26.120 --> 19:28.120
What are you going to do?

19:30.020 --> 19:31.490
What?

19:36.130 --> 19:38.360
So it’s yellow?

19:38.360 --> 19:39.680
A good color, huh?

19:39.680 --> 19:41.600
The color of happiness.

19:41.600 --> 19:42.740
I’m sorry.

19:42.740 --> 19:45.250
I’m the one who got it in curry.

19:45.250 --> 19:47.300
But I’m the one who got it dirty.

19:47.300 --> 19:50.510
I’m the one who tipped the pot.

19:50.510 --> 19:52.180
It’s not your fault.

19:52.930 --> 19:54.440
Itsumi-san...

20:02.590 --> 20:04.770
Now, then... Let’s eat!

20:04.770 --> 20:06.780
I’m starving!

20:06.780 --> 20:09.160
Mamoru, set the table, already.

20:09.160 --> 20:10.270
You’re such a kid.

20:10.270 --> 20:11.440
What?

20:11.440 --> 20:13.020
Jeez...

20:21.130 --> 20:22.890
It smells like curry.

20:24.470 --> 20:26.280
Oh, Itsumi.

20:26.280 --> 20:27.370
Thanks for today.

20:27.370 --> 20:29.630
The pickled potatoes, the cheese omelet,

20:29.630 --> 20:32.310
the Japanese Salisbury steak...
They were all really good.

20:32.310 --> 20:35.740
Especially the potatoes today!

20:35.740 --> 20:38.160
Ayako-san made those.

20:38.160 --> 20:40.510
I see.

20:40.510 --> 20:43.110
But they tasted just like yours.

20:43.110 --> 20:44.390
I’m sure they did.

20:44.390 --> 20:45.890
I taught her my recipe.

20:45.890 --> 20:47.890
I see.

20:49.760 --> 20:51.090
What?

20:51.090 --> 20:52.030
There’s no room.

20:52.030 --> 20:54.020
I’m tired.

20:54.020 --> 20:56.480
I think I’ll sleep here.

20:56.480 --> 20:58.140
Why?

20:58.140 --> 20:59.650
Jeez.

21:02.190 --> 21:07.750
<i>When I’m next to Mamoru, I feel at peace.</i>

21:08.820 --> 21:12.920
<i>Is this the power of beatrice?</i>

21:15.440 --> 21:16.940
Brother?

21:18.700 --> 21:21.970
No... Hey, Mamoru.

21:21.970 --> 21:25.220
